  "answer": "This feature request has been made before. The main tracking issue is PowerToys#46333 (Privacy Overlay). It proposes a way to exclude chosen windows from screen sharing, recording and screenshots, using a hotkey like Always on Top. #48566 was closed as a duplicate of #46333. #34950 (Window Masking) asks for the same thing and was closed against #13035, even though a commenter pointed out that #13035 is a different feature. No PowerToys utility does this yet. Subscribe to #46333 and add your use case there (permanently excluding Outlook and Teams windows). Until a feature ships, share a single window or app instead of the whole screen in Teams, or close sensitive apps before you share. A proof of concept exists in #46333 that uses SetWindowDisplayAffinity with WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE."
